597			<section aria-labelledby="examples">
598				<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>
599				<article class="card">
600					<h3>Component Cards</h3>
601					<p>Card components are useful for organizing related content. They include a subtle border and padding for visual separation.</p>
602					<a class="button" href="#resources">Learn more<span class="visually-hidden"> about accessibility resources</span></a>
603				</article>
604	
605				<article class="card">
606					<h3>Interactive Elements</h3>
607					<p>Buttons and links are fully accessible with clear focus states. All interactive elements include visible focus indicators and proper ARIA labels.</p>
608					<p><strong>Keyboard navigation:</strong> Use <kbd>Tab</kbd> to move forward, <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd> to move backward, and <kbd>Enter</kbd> to activate.</p>
609				</article>
610	
611				<article class="card">
612					<h3>Accessible Form</h3>
613					<form id="contact-form" novalidate>
614						<p class="form-hint">Fields marked * are required.</p>
615						<div class="field">
616							<label for="email">Email <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
617							<input type="email" id="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" inputmode="email" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="none" required aria-describedby="email-help">
618							<span id="email-error" class="error-message"></span>
619							<small id="email-help" class="form-hint">For example, name@example.com</small>
620						</div>
621						<div class="field">
622							<label for="message">Message</label>
623							<textarea id="message" name="message" rows="4" maxlength="2000" aria-describedby="message-help"></textarea>
624							<small id="message-help" class="form-hint">Up to 2,000 characters. <span id="message-count">2,000</span> remaining.</small>
625						</div>
626						<button type="submit">Send message</button>
627						<p id="form-status" role="status"></p>
628					</form>
629				</article>
630	
631				<article class="card">
632					<h3>Live Region Example</h3>
633					<p>Click the button to announce a message using a live region. This demonstrates how screen readers are notified of dynamic updates.</p>
634					<button id="announce" type="button">Announce message</button>
635					<div class="live-region" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
636						<span id="live-message"></span>
637					</div>
638				</article>
